Simple commit-message convention
Use this pattern:

type(scope): summary
Examples:

fix(ui): slow touch repeat rate
fix(eeprom): initialize fresh-board temp defaults
fix(sensor): only update temp min/max when changed
refactor(ui): decouple manual run state from main screen
feat(config): add temp dwell adjustment
Recommended types:

fix = bug fix
feat = new behavior
refactor = code cleanup / reorg
chore = non-functional maintenance
docs = comments / notes / docs
Recommended scope:

ui
eeprom
sensor
actuator
config
cycle
main
A short rule:

1 line summary
optional body only if needed
keep it to the point
Example:

fix(ui): remove touch timer reset in interval updater
Minimal changelog format
Keep a simple file such as CHANGELOG.md with entries like:

Changelog
Unreleased
fix(ui): slow touch repeat rate for held inputs
fix(eeprom): initialize fresh-board defaults for temp delay and min temp
fix(sensor): only write temp min/max when values actually change
2026-09-07
refactor(ui): simplify touch detection and state handling
fix(cycle): separate manual cycle state from main auto-cycle state
fix(actuator): improve abort/shake sequencing
This is enough for a small embedded project and stays easy to maintain.